 "notes_path": "history/polities/_notes/me-02.md",
 "problems": [
  "Cross-dossier conflicts left for the reviewer, details in the notes: elam (me-01) books an Assyrian occupation/annexation of Susiana -653..-612 that the Ashurbanipal page contradicts (no Elam mirror in neo-assyrian-empire); elam Kurigalzu II c. -1320 occupation vs babylonia Kurigalzu I c. -1350 (Kurigalzu II page: the conquest \"now tends to be assigned to the earlier king\"); elam -1158 gain and -1153 loss of Babylonia vs babylonia -1155/-1153; elam occupation_end Eshnunna -1760 vs eshnunna -1764 and dissolve -1762; third-dynasty-of-ur loss of Eshnunna -2020 vs eshnunna found -2026; larsa has no loss of Uruk at -1865 and names Uruk as free text; greek-city-states Cyprus -700 vs neo-assyrian-empire gain -709; scythia books its vassal tie itself (neo-assyrian-empire now carries the suzerain side).",
  "Cliopatria row twenty-sixth-dynasty-of-egypt starts -615 but Psamtik's independence is c. -655 and the Delta vassalage from -664 (me-03 should start it at -664 or -655). Cliopatria Assyrian Egypt (-650, -630) is the whole Neo-Assyrian Empire again and is marked wrong in assyrian-egypt; the map should drop that row for -654..-616.",
  "Assyria and neo-assyrian-empire are one continuous state in the Assyria article (split at -912/-911 only because Cliopatria has two rows): the colour agent may give both one colour. Assyria Wikidata Q41137 is shared with the Cliopatria row Syria (1973..2024), a wrong id on that row. Cliopatria Assyria -1800 has no Mari, so the -1796 Mari gain adds land the keyframe lacks.",
